# VIVA QUESTIONS WITH ANSWERS

# ==========================================

1. What is Salesforce?
   Salesforce is a cloud-based CRM platform used to manage customers, applications, and business processes.

2. What is CRM?
   CRM stands for Customer Relationship Management.
   It is used to manage customer data and interactions.

3. What is a custom object?
   A custom object is a user-created database table in Salesforce.

4. Difference between standard object and custom object?
   Standard objects are prebuilt by Salesforce.
   Custom objects are created by users.

5. What is Object Manager?
   Object Manager is used to create and manage objects, fields, and relationships.

6. What is a field in Salesforce?
   A field stores individual data values inside an object.

7. What is a record?
   A record is a single row of data in an object.

8. What is Lookup Relationship?
   Lookup relationship connects two objects.

9. Why is Lookup used in Tenant object?
   To connect Tenant with Property object.

10. What is a tab?
    A tab provides access to object records in Salesforce UI.

11. What is Lightning App?
    A Lightning App is a collection of tabs and functionalities grouped together.

12. What is a report?
    A report displays organized data from Salesforce objects.

13. What is a dashboard?
    A dashboard visually represents report data using charts and graphs.

14. Difference between report and dashboard?
    Report shows data in tabular form.
    Dashboard shows graphical visualization.

15. What are components in dashboard?
    Charts, tables, and graphs used to display report data.

16. What is cloud computing?
    Cloud computing provides computing resources over the internet.

17. Is Salesforce SaaS, PaaS, or IaaS?
    Salesforce mainly provides SaaS and PaaS services.

18. What is SaaS?
    Software provided over internet without installation.

19. What is PaaS?
    Platform provided for application development and deployment.

20. Advantages of Salesforce?
    Easy access, cloud storage, automation, scalability, and security.

21. What is App Launcher?
    App Launcher is used to open Salesforce apps and modules.

22. What is dashboard refresh?
    Updating dashboard data from latest reports.

23. Why reports are important?
    Reports help analyze and organize data.

24. What is cloud CRM?
    CRM software hosted on cloud infrastructure.

25. What is multitenancy in Salesforce?
    Multiple users share same cloud infrastructure securely.
